# App preferences capture-settings records, beyond System Settings.
# One line per preferences domain (usually the app's bundle id), then the
# top-level keys to keep; `*` and `?` match like shell globs. Only listed keys
# are captured: whole domains hold licence keys, window positions, timestamps
# and network names, and this repository is public.
# Find a setting's key with `nix run .#settings-watch -- <domain>`.

# Bartender: menu bar behaviour and which items are shown or hidden. Its
# licence (license6*) and triggers (they name Wi-Fi networks) stay out.
com.surteesstudios.Bartender BartenderBarOnlyOnNotchScreens HideItemsWhenShowingOthers HideShownItemsLeaveItemsToRightOfBartender HideShownItemsWhen MenuBarShape MenuBarStyle MouseExitDelay OptionClickBartenderIconShows ProfileSettings ReduceMenuItemSpacing SeperatePills ShiftClickShowsAllItems ShowAllItemsWhenDragging ShowDivider SimpleLayoutModeEnabled UseBartenderBar bartenderAutoExtendsMenuBar

